#RingCtrl8 1
#RingCtrl9 1

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example uses Events to simulate a hill-climb and switch powertrains during the course of the simulation.
#
#In this example, a 2WD pickup truck attempts to climb a steep off-road hill. Browse to the Vehicle: Assembly screen and click on the blue link for the powertrain to see that the vehicle has RWD only.
#
#As the truck climbs the hill tire traction is lost, the rear wheels spin, and the vehicle becomes stuck. When the truck starts to roll backwards the throttle is closed and the transmission is shifted into neutral. At this point the drivetrain is shifted into 4WD and engages low range (2:1 ratio) in the transfer case. This is accomplished by replacing the entire powertrain dataset linked to the run. Once this happens the additional traction provided by the now-driven front tires allows the truck to successfully to climb the hill.
#
#When using Events, any output variable or equation can be set as a trigger. When some threshold level of a trigger is reached (either increasing or decreasing), any aspect of the run can be changed. Changes may include control methods (i.e., from open loop to closed loop or vice versa), model parameters, or definition of the environment.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

